Add a Background Graphic to the Frame
You can add a background graphic to the background of the Frame.
To add a graphic to the background of a Frame:
Add a Background Graphic to the Frame
Plant Simulation Help 10-111
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Drag a .gif, .bmp, .ppm, .ppm raw, .dgn, .dxf, or a .dwg file from the Windows Explorer or the Internet
Browser over the background of the Frame and drop it there.
• Drag a layout drawing over the background of the Frame and drop it there.
You can use this layout drawing as the actual background of the Frame and insert the Plant Simulation
objects on top of it. This is feasible when your simulation model is not too complex.
Note
If you are modeling a complex plant, this might not be practicable, as it might lead to a very cluttered
layout.
Be aware that the .dxf, .dgn or .dwg files are vector-based, whereas Plant Simulation uses pixel-based
graphics. This means that you have to think about how to transfer one size to the other.
If the CAD-drawing contains units and its dimension is not greater than 32000 by 32000 pixels, Plant
Simulation automatically uses a Corrective Scaling of 1.
Add a Background Graphic to the Frame
10-112 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If the CAD-drawing contains units and its dimension is greater than 32000 by 32000 pixels, Plant
Simulation scales the drawing so that it fits into the Frame window.
The Console window shows the origin of the dwg drawing and the dimension of the drawing.
Compare Add a JT Layout File to Your Simulation Model
Compare Import a 3D Graphic
Compare Add a Point Cloud
