Work with Objects in the Frame Window
You can manipulate the objects, simulation objects as well as vector graphics you drew and inserted into
the Frame.
• To open the object or the Frame window, double-click the object or a Frame in the model Frame,
MyPlantAnytown in our sample model.
• To insert an object in the Frame, select the object in the Class Library or the Toolbox, drag it over the
Frame window and drop it there.
• To show or hide the grid in the Frame window, click 
 . Showing the grid makes it easier to insert
an object at exactly the position you need it to be at.
• To select an object, click it with the left mouse button. You can then move it in the Frame by dragging
the mouse.
• To nudge the selected object one pixel at a time in a direction, press the respective arrow keys on the
keyboard. To move the selected object one grid unit at a time, press Shift+ the respective arrow key.
• To deselect a selected object, click another object or click anywhere in the Frame.
Work with Objects in the Frame Window
Plant Simulation Help 10-117
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To select more than one object in a Frame at a time, hold down Shift, and click the objects you want to
mark or drag a marquee over the objects: Hold the left mouse button down, and drag the mouse over
the objects, making sure the marquee encloses all of them, and then release the mouse button. You can
also combine both methods.
To select all objects in the Frame window, press Ctrl+A.
• To search for any object in the Frame window, click Incremental Find Object on the Frame ribbon tab
and start typing its name. Plant Simulation then finds and selects the object.
• To connect objects, use the Connector. The Connector displays handles 
  after you select it. Click a
handle to change its shape, i.e., to make the Connector longer or shorter or to move the anchor point up
or down.
• To show or hide connections between objects which you established with the Connector, click 
  on
the View ribbon tab.
• To show objects that are not connected to another object, click 
  on the Frame ribbon tab.
• To zoom the contents of the Frame in, roll the mouse wheel forward.
• To zoom the contents of the Frame out, roll the mouse wheel backward.
• To show or hide the names of the objects you inserted into the Frame, click 
 .
Work with Objects in the Frame Window
10-118 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To prevent another user from modifying the structure of the model, click 
 .
• To edit the icons of the Frame, and to add animation structures to it, click 
  on the Home ribbon tab.
• To model transitions between Frames use the Interface. When you connect Frames, which have several
Interfaces, with objects, Plant Simulation opens the dialog Select Interface. Select the Interface the
Connector attaches to and click OK.
Note
If a sub-Frame only contains a single object, you can also connect the sub-Frame without having to
use Interfaces.
• To open the Frame you double-click and to close the Frame it is contained in, press Shift and double-
click a Frame located within a Frame.
• To move down in the hierarchy of Frames, closing the active Frame, and opening the next Frame one
level down in the structure, select Down one Level on the context menu.
• To open the window of the Frame from which the current Frame has derived, click Open Origin 
  on
the Home ribbon tab.
• To close the active Frame and open its location, click Open Location 
• To assign the different states a Frame can be in, use the attributes StateBlocked, StateEntryShut,
StateResourceMissing, StateSetup, StateWorking, Stopped, and Unplanned. Plant Simulation shows
the state of the object as a colored ring on a pole by default.
Color Means that the Frame is
red Failed
pink Stopped
blue Paused
light blue Unplanned
green Working
yellow Blocked
brown Setting-Up
cyan recovering or has a closed entrance
orange Waiting for a resource (Exporter)
• To open help for the selected object, press F1.
