Delete Parts with the Mouse or when Resetting the Model
You can delete parts with the mouse or when resetting the simulation model.
To delete one, several or all MUs, do one of the following:
• Select a single MU you would like to delete and press Delete.
• To delete all MUs in all objects in the active Frame and its sub-Frames, click 
  Delete MUs on the
Home ribbon tab.
• To delete all mobile objects (MUs), when you reset the simulation model by clicking the Reset
Simulation button or by calling the method reset, you can enter deleteMovables into a Method,
which you name reset and which you insert into your simulation model.
Note
If you simulation model still contains parts, meaning that Plant Simulation does not start counting
parts with 1, for example .MUs.Part:1, for a new simulation run, check if the model contains additional
Frames with inserted EventControllers. Reset the EventControllers there as well.
